From 54f2794428586b3d877bc98c404eab55091f0e55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 13:00:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dynarmic A32: dead flags at a block's exit are not stored; a
 conditional branch tests its compare

A block ending in links (B<cond>'s If terminal, a branch, a call, the next instruction) reads the
ARM code its successors start with (TranslateArm, FlagsLookahead): along every path, following
branches and calls (BL into the called code), an instruction that reads a flag not set again yet
on that path makes the flags live; one that sets them all ends the path; a return, a jump or call
through a register, SVC, MRS/MSR or anything unknown counts as a read; a branch target reached
again with no more flags unset adds no path; 64 instructions and 6 branches at most. When the
flags are dead (IR::Block::nzcv_dead_at_exit), A32DeadNZCVPass drops the flag stores after the
block's last flag read, and for an If terminal appends CondFlagsSub32/Add32/Test32/NZ32 (the
compare's values: CMP/SUBS, CMN/ADDS, TST, a value's N and Z) as the block's last instruction:
`cmp a, b` and the branch on the host's flags (EmitCond), instead of cmc/lahf/seto, the store,
the load and sahf/cmc. The code read is added to the block's ranges for invalidation.
UserConfig::elide_dead_nzcv (Eden: on); off with cycle counting and halts on memory accesses.

Host harness with Eden's options, fastmem, valgrind's instruction count: Mario Kart 8 Deluxe's
hottest loops (fill, copy, byte copy, test chain, indexed copy) 760 -> 536 an iteration, a C
benchmark of game-like code (clang -O2, ARM) 135,555 -> 126,310 a frame; calls, PUSH/POP and
struct accesses unchanged (their loops end before an SVC). Old vs new: 3,200 random A32 programs
equal (gen2/3/4/7/9 and gen10, flags across blocks; ARM and Thumb, fastmem, split stack).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
