     bool inline_conditional_instructions = false;
 
+    /// A block reads the ARM code its successors start with (a few instructions, along their
+    /// branches): when they set the condition flags before reading them, the flags the block ends
+    /// with are dead. It then doesn't store them, and a conditional branch at its end tests the
+    /// compare's values on the host directly (cmp; jcc) instead of the stored flags. ARM code
+    /// only; calls are taken to clobber the flags (as the procedure call standard has it), returns
+    /// and indirect jumps to read them. Off with cycle counting and with halts on memory accesses.
+    bool elide_dead_nzcv = false;
+
